From fd8599515cbd9045b340a36b9b1ed38beabf6faf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Implementer)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:05:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(spacebar): right off-centered template is the
 default file, the left position is its mirror

DEFAULT_SPACEBAR_OFF_CENTERED is now stabilzer_spacebar_off-center_right.stl; off-centered-left is that template mirrored in its own coordinates (exact integer matrix, before the rotation). The sections of both positions are identical to the previous output; docs, tests, config example and AGENTS.md follow.
---
 AGENTS.md                        |  2 +-
 CHANGELOG.md                     |  2 +-
 README.md                        | 24 +++++++--------
 ROADMAP.md                       |  2 +-
 fat_plate_config.example.toml    |  6 ++--
 fat_plate_generator.py           | 36 +++++++++++------------
 tests/test_cutout_orientation.py | 50 ++++++++++++++++----------------
 7 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 0c966d9..99cf637 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ python .\tools\preview.py plate.stl --layout my_layout.json --output plate.png
 
 - Keine Werte runden, auf ein Raster snappen oder glätten. Alles bleibt präzise und exakt. Ungenauigkeiten werden an der Quelle behoben (Blender-Dateien, Templates), nicht im Code kaschiert. Mängel in Templates im Bericht melden, nicht verstecken.
 - Transformationsreihenfolge: Rotation je Stabilizer um dessen Switch-Zentrum, dann Gesamttransformation um den Ursprung, dann Verschiebung, sodass die Bounding-Box bei (0, 0) beginnt. Rotationen und Spiegelung sind exakte Integer-Matrizen auf den 2D-Daten, es entstehen keine gespiegelten CAD-Körper.
-- Die Stabilizer-Ausschnitte werden nur gedreht, nie gespiegelt (die Spiegelung der Ganzplatten-Transformation gilt nur für Tasten und Plattenumriss). Eine Ausnahme gibt es: die rechte Off-Center-Spacebar (`--spacebar-position off-centered-right`) ist das gespiegelte linke Template, als exakte Integer-Matrix im Template-Koordinatensystem vor der Rotation; es entsteht kein gespiegelter CAD-Körper.
+- Die Stabilizer-Ausschnitte werden nur gedreht, nie gespiegelt (die Spiegelung der Ganzplatten-Transformation gilt nur für Tasten und Plattenumriss). Eine Ausnahme gibt es: die linke Off-Center-Spacebar (`--spacebar-position off-centered-left`) ist das gespiegelte rechte Template, als exakte Integer-Matrix im Template-Koordinatensystem vor der Rotation; es entsteht kein gespiegelter CAD-Körper.
 - Die Orientierungs-Defaults stehen zentral in `OrientationConfig`. Die Werte hat der Nutzer nach Sichtprüfung festgelegt; nicht ohne Auftrag ändern.
 - Die exportierte STL wird nur im Speicher geprüft, nie repariert, nach Komponenten gefiltert oder neu exportiert.
 - Socket, Stabilizer und Spacebar laufen durch denselben Code. Keine Sonderwege je Template, keine stille Glättung von Schrägen, keine Konturen weglassen.
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 19faa16..6a7306c 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ All notable changes to this project are documented in this file.
 - `parse_kle()` reads the properties of a key like the Keyboard Layout Editor: `w`, `h`, `x2`, `y2`, `w2`, `h2` and `l` apply to the next key and are reset only after a key, so several objects in a row before one key add up (`{"w": 2}, {"c": "#fff"}, "A"` gives A the width 2); `w` also sets `w2` and `h` also sets `h2` unless the same object names them. Single objects before a key give the same result as before (ISO Enter, stepped Caps Lock).
 - Decals (`"d": true`) are ignored: they get no footprint and no cutout, but the position moves on by their width. No layout in `kle-jsons/` has decals.
 - `r`, `rx` and `ry` anywhere but on the first item of a row are an error (`ValueError` naming the row) instead of being read silently wrong. KLE exports do not produce this.
-- The right off-centered spacebar is the left template mirrored instead of a second file. The mirror is an exact integer matrix in the template's own coordinates, applied before the stabilizer rotation (so it matches the former right file for every rotation); it is the only cutout that is mirrored, and `PlateModel.mirrored` records it per key. The plate is unchanged apart from float noise in the templates (`centered` and `off-centered-left` byte-identical). `TemplateSet` has one field `spacebar_off_centered` (the left file) instead of two, and `TemplateSet.spacebar_for()` is the single place that maps a position to a file and a mirror flag. `stabilzer_spacebar_off-center_right.stl` stays in the repository but is no longer read.
+- The left off-centered spacebar is the right template mirrored instead of a second file. The mirror is an exact integer matrix in the template's own coordinates, applied before the stabilizer rotation (so it matches the former left file for every rotation); it is the only cutout that is mirrored, and `PlateModel.mirrored` records it per key. The plate is unchanged apart from float noise in the templates (`centered` byte-identical; the sections of `off-centered-left` and `off-centered-right` are identical, only the triangulation of the STL differs). `TemplateSet` has one field `spacebar_off_centered` (the right file) instead of two, and `TemplateSet.spacebar_for()` is the single place that maps a position to a file and a mirror flag. `stabilzer_spacebar_off-center_left.stl` stays in the repository but is no longer read. A custom file given with `--spacebar-off-centered` (or `templates.spacebar_off_centered`) is now taken as the RIGHT design.
 - `--spacebar-off-centered` and the config key `templates.spacebar_off_centered` replace `--spacebar-off-centered-left` / `--spacebar-off-centered-right` and `spacebar_off_centered_left` / `spacebar_off_centered_right`. The old names are not kept as aliases and are refused as unknown.
 - `generate()` and `build_plate_model()` take a `Settings` object (with a `TemplateSet` for the template paths) instead of long parameter lists: `build_plate_model(kle_path, settings)` and `generate(kle_path, settings, output, config_path=None)`. The generated STL is byte-identical to before (checked for the orientation test layout, the 40% layout and the stepped Caps Lock with `--stepped-key wide-caps`).
 - The command line options that a config can also set have no built-in default in the parser any more (that is how a given option is told from a missing one); the help texts still name the defaults.
